1646
01:05:36,725 --> 01:05:38,977
-So much for our movie pitch.
-At least we're alive.

1647
01:05:39,060 --> 01:05:40,854
Hey, Caleb, you are quite a negotiator.

1648
01:05:40,937 --> 01:05:42,147
-Yeah.
-Wow.

1649
01:05:42,230 --> 01:05:44,024
-It's all here.
-(OVERLAPPING CONVERSATIONS)

1650
01:05:44,107 --> 01:05:45,233
Hey. (SNAPS FINGERS)

1651
01:05:45,317 --> 01:05:47,694
-Kill them.
-GAIL: Wait, what?

1652
01:05:47,777 --> 01:05:49,446
Wait, wait, wait... No, no, no, no, no.

1653
01:05:49,529 --> 01:05:50,864
-Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.
-(GAIL GROANS)

1654
01:05:50,947 --> 01:05:52,657
We should have anticipated
that they'd come back

1655
01:05:52,741 --> 01:05:53,742
and get their guns again.

1656
01:05:53,825 --> 01:05:55,952
Yeah. Don't blame yourself.
I missed it, too.

1657
01:05:56,036 --> 01:05:58,246
These guys are
professional killers, right?

1658
01:05:58,330 --> 01:05:59,623
-We both missed it.
-SLATTERY: We all missed it.

1659
01:05:59,706 --> 01:06:01,416
-CALEB: Yeah.
-I'm kicking myself now.

1660
01:06:01,499 --> 01:06:02,834
VINCENT: It was right in my face.

1661
01:06:02,918 --> 01:06:04,628
(WHISPERS) Hey, Slattery, now would be
a good time to pull off

1662
01:06:04,711 --> 01:06:05,712
some of those moves.

1663
01:06:05,795 --> 01:06:07,130
I told you, I can't... I can't do it.

1664
01:06:07,213 --> 01:06:08,715
Real violence makes me throw up.

1665
01:06:08,798 --> 01:06:13,637
John, no flying machine
will ever fly from New York to Paris.

1666
01:06:13,720 --> 01:06:16,139
-What?
-Orville Wright said that.

1667
01:06:16,973 --> 01:06:18,600
Now, do you understand what I'm saying?

1668
01:06:19,184 --> 01:06:20,602
Yeah.

1669
01:06:20,685 --> 01:06:21,978
Yeah, I understand.

1670
01:06:23,063 --> 01:06:24,356
Stand back, everybody.

1671
01:06:24,439 --> 01:06:25,899
-I got this.
-GAIL: Okay.

1672
01:06:25,982 --> 01:06:27,943
SLATTERY: Fellas, fellas. (LAUGHS)

1673
01:06:28,026 --> 01:06:30,028
Nobody wants to get hurt, right?

1674
01:06:30,111 --> 01:06:31,738
So why don't we just handle it like this?

1675
01:06:31,821 --> 01:06:33,573
-(GRUNTS)
-(GAIL GASPS)

1676
01:06:34,282 --> 01:06:35,617
-(GUN FIRES)
-(ALL EXCLAIM)

1677
01:06:35,700 --> 01:06:36,952
-Whoa!
-(GRUNTS)

1678
01:06:37,035 --> 01:06:38,495
(UPBEAT COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING)

1679
01:06:38,578 --> 01:06:39,955
-Hi-yah!
-(GRUNTS)

1680
01:06:40,997 --> 01:06:41,998
(SLATTERY LAUGHS)

1681
01:06:42,082 --> 01:06:44,042
-Hey, hey, hey.
-(LAUGHS) Not bad, right?

1682
01:06:45,835 --> 01:06:47,963
Hey, boys. Come on!

1683
01:06:48,505 --> 01:06:49,714
(GRUNTING)

1684
01:06:50,382 --> 01:06:51,466
Take that.

1685
01:06:52,425 --> 01:06:54,344
-Too slow.
-(GRUNTS)

1686
01:06:54,427 --> 01:06:56,012
-Good job.
-SLATTERY: Nope.

1687
01:06:56,096 --> 01:06:57,973
(GRUNTING)

1688
01:06:59,391 --> 01:07:01,810
-What the fuck?
-(YELLS)

1689
01:07:02,394 --> 01:07:03,561
Consider that a divorce.

1690
01:07:03,645 --> 01:07:05,939
-Hey, you're mine!
-SLATTERY: You want some, too, baldy?

1691
01:07:06,564 --> 01:07:07,941
-Take that.
-(YELLS)

1692
01:07:08,024 --> 01:07:09,734
This is fun. I can do this all day.

1693
01:07:11,027 --> 01:07:12,237
Got your eye, motherfucker.

1694
01:07:12,320 --> 01:07:13,238
-(SQUELCHES)
-(SCREAMING)

1695
01:07:13,321 --> 01:07:14,197
ALL: Ooh!

1696
01:07:14,781 --> 01:07:16,199
Going up, motherfucker.

1697
01:07:16,282 --> 01:07:17,367
I got you, asshole!

1698
01:07:17,450 --> 01:07:19,035
-(GRUNTS)
-(SCREAMS)

1699
01:07:20,120 --> 01:07:21,329
(ALL EXCLAIM)

1700
01:07:21,413 --> 01:07:23,206
Down goes Frazier.

1701
01:07:23,289 --> 01:07:24,541
Slattery, you old son of a bitch.

1702
01:07:24,624 --> 01:07:26,710
-(RETCHES)
-(ALL GROAN)

1703
01:07:26,793 --> 01:07:27,627
Oh!

1704
01:07:27,711 --> 01:07:29,421
-Still got it.
-(ALL GASP)

1705
01:07:30,296 --> 01:07:32,507
This is for Nico and Marco

1706
01:07:32,590 --> 01:07:34,259
and all the unnecessary agita
you caused me

1707
01:07:34,342 --> 01:07:35,760
over the last 11 and a half hours.

1708
01:07:35,844 --> 01:07:37,220
-No, no, no, no.
-You kill my friends,

1709
01:07:37,303 --> 01:07:39,389
I kill your friends. Bye-bye.

1710
01:07:39,472 --> 01:07:41,391
GAIL: No, no, no, no. Please, please.

1711
01:07:41,474 --> 01:07:42,392
Huh?

1712
01:07:42,475 --> 01:07:43,935
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1713
01:07:46,312 --> 01:07:48,231
-(YELLS)
-Stings.

1714
01:07:49,399 --> 01:07:51,443
-(NOTE PLAYS)
-(CLINKS)

1715
01:07:55,447 --> 01:07:57,115
-Whoops.
-Let's face it.

1716
01:07:57,198 --> 01:07:59,200
You can pack quite a punch.
"Let's face it."

1717
01:07:59,284 --> 01:08:00,744
(ALL CHUCKLING)

1718
01:08:00,827 --> 01:08:01,661
-(VOICES OVERLAPPING)
-OTTO: Wow.

1719
01:08:01,745 --> 01:08:02,912
VINCENT: Where did you learn that, man?

1720
01:08:02,996 --> 01:08:05,665
SLATTERY:
I'm self-taught. Totally self-taught.

1721
01:08:06,249 --> 01:08:08,918
-I have a practice head in my garage.
-GAIL: Did you see that? He saved my life.

1722
01:08:09,002 --> 01:08:10,712
-I gotta tell you...
-OTTO: Unreal.

1723
01:08:10,795 --> 01:08:12,047
Oh, shit.

1724
01:08:12,130 --> 01:08:13,757
(OMINOUS WESTERN MUSIC PLAYING)

1725
01:08:17,802 --> 01:08:18,678
SLATTERY: Ding-ding.

1726
01:08:19,512 --> 01:08:21,264
Round two, motherfuckers.

1727
01:08:21,347 --> 01:08:22,807
I'll take 'em one by one.

1728
01:08:24,768 --> 01:08:25,810
(GUNS FIRING)

1729
01:08:30,732 --> 01:08:32,442
-(EXHALES)
-(CROWS CAWING)

1730
01:08:32,525 --> 01:08:34,861
Wow, I thought that was
gonna take much more time and energy.

1731
01:08:34,944 --> 01:08:36,780
Yeah, you know, we just picked
up those dead guys' guns.

1732
01:08:36,863 --> 01:08:38,406
-We just went for it.
-Improvised a little.

1733
01:08:38,490 --> 01:08:39,491
VINCENT: The guns make it easier.

1734
01:08:39,574 --> 01:08:40,784
I've never shot a gun before in my life.

1735
01:08:40,867 --> 01:08:42,577
-GAIL: Thank you.
-I would have never guessed.

1736
01:08:43,870 --> 01:08:45,622
-Damn it.
-Get her!

1737
01:08:50,960 --> 01:08:53,379
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

1738
01:08:53,463 --> 01:08:54,839
-Tom? I have to call you back.
-TOM: Gail.

1739
01:08:54,923 --> 01:08:56,132
I was able to extend the deposit.

1740
01:08:56,216 --> 01:08:58,384
We'll talk about this later.
I'm literally in the middle of a thing.

1741
01:08:58,468 --> 01:08:59,469
I have to call you back.

1742
01:08:59,552 --> 01:09:01,096
Are you on a treadmill right now?

1743
01:09:01,179 --> 01:09:03,223
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

1744
01:09:09,020 --> 01:09:10,188
GAIL: Get back here!

1745
01:09:10,939 --> 01:09:12,148
-(GRUNTS)
-(YELLS)

1746
01:09:15,735 --> 01:09:20,240
Hey, give us one good reason
why we shouldn't kill you... right now.

1747
01:09:20,323 --> 01:09:22,909
-I have very powerful friends.
-Uh-huh.

1748
01:09:22,992 --> 01:09:24,494
-We can make a deal.
-GAIL: Like what?

1749
01:09:24,577 --> 01:09:26,037
Let me explain.

1750
01:09:26,913 --> 01:09:28,289
-What do you guys think?
-ALL: Yeah, yeah.

1751
01:09:28,373 --> 01:09:29,582
-Yeah, give her a shot.
-You sure?

1752
01:09:29,666 --> 01:09:30,959
-OTTO: Yeah.
-Yeah, let her explain. Let her explain.

1753
01:09:32,627 --> 01:09:35,380
-We're listening.
-Okay. What if...

1754
01:09:35,463 --> 01:09:36,798
-(GRUNTS)
-GAIL: Caleb!

1755
01:09:36,881 --> 01:09:39,175
We just said that
we would listen to what she has to say.

1756
01:09:39,259 --> 01:09:41,469
I'm sorry.
It's the adrenaline. I just had to do it.

1757
01:09:41,553 --> 01:09:43,847
Okay. Continue, uh...

1758
01:09:43,930 --> 01:09:46,349
-Ludovica.
-That is so pretty.

1759
01:09:46,432 --> 01:09:47,725
-Thank you. (GRUNTS)
-GAIL: I've never heard that...

1760
01:09:47,809 --> 01:09:48,768
Vincent. What did I just say?

1761
01:09:48,852 --> 01:09:51,146
I know, but you saw what they
tried to do to us back there.

1762
01:09:51,229 --> 01:09:53,690
-She tried to kill us all.
-We said that we would at least listen

1763
01:09:53,773 --> 01:09:55,400
-to what she has to propose...
-(GRUNTS)

1764
01:09:55,483 --> 01:09:58,236
-Guys, what is going on?
-Why don't they listen to you?

1765
01:09:58,319 --> 01:09:59,696
Ludovica, just let me...

1766
01:09:59,779 --> 01:10:02,282
You're already on thin ice,
so just shut up for a second, okay?

1767
01:10:02,365 --> 01:10:04,075
-Otto, don't hit her.
-Yeah? Sorry. Yeah.

1768
01:10:04,159 --> 01:10:05,160
-Slattery.
-What?

1769
01:10:05,243 --> 01:10:06,911
Do you need to get one in before
we can listen to what she has to say?

1770
01:10:06,995 --> 01:10:08,663
No. I'm good.
I got all mine out back there.

1771
01:10:08,746 --> 01:10:10,206
Okay. Everybody chill?

1772
01:10:10,290 --> 01:10:12,125
-Yeah.
-Yeah, I'm super chill. Super chill.

1773
01:10:12,208 --> 01:10:13,543
-Ludovica.
-Yes?

1774
01:10:13,626 --> 01:10:16,713
-The floor is yours.
-Really? Now?

1775
01:10:17,505 --> 01:10:21,342
-Okay? So, if you let me go...
-(GRUNTS) Oh!

1776
01:10:21,426 --> 01:10:23,803
Guys, what in the actual fuck?

1777
01:10:24,512 --> 01:10:27,056
(ALL EXCLAIMING)

1778
01:10:27,140 --> 01:10:30,643
-(YELLS)
-(GUN CLICKING)

1779
01:10:31,311 --> 01:10:32,478
You're all out.

1780
01:10:34,564 --> 01:10:36,232
Wait. Wait.

1781
01:10:36,316 --> 01:10:37,275
(GRUNTS)

1782
01:10:37,358 --> 01:10:38,860
(YELLS)

1783
01:10:38,943 --> 01:10:41,863
-(GRUNTING)
-(ALL EXCLAIMING)

1784
01:10:44,282 --> 01:10:46,576
Huh? You like that? (GRUNTING)

1785
01:10:48,036 --> 01:10:49,662
(SCREAMS, GRUNTS)

1786
01:10:49,746 --> 01:10:52,957
-(ALL CLAMORING)
-(GRUNTING)

1787
01:10:53,458 --> 01:10:56,669
-(RETCHES)
-(SCREAMING)

1788
01:10:56,753 --> 01:11:00,423
All right, all right.
All right, you did it. You're good.

1789
01:11:00,506 --> 01:11:02,550
(PANTING)

1790
01:11:04,219 --> 01:11:06,137
-Oh, my God.
-OTTO: Gail.

1791
01:11:07,096 --> 01:11:08,389
She said, "Wait." Why did you...

1792
01:11:08,473 --> 01:11:10,350
I got swept up in it, too. What can I say?

1793
01:11:10,433 --> 01:11:13,353
I'm human. I'm not perfect.

1794
01:11:13,436 --> 01:11:15,855
Of course. Of course.
No, we're not judging.

1795
01:11:15,939 --> 01:11:17,148
Jeez.

1796
01:11:18,983 --> 01:11:20,693
Let's finish what we started, huh?

1797
01:11:21,319 --> 01:11:23,696
(UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING)

1798
01:11:23,780 --> 01:11:25,281
-You guys ready?
-GAIL: Yes!

1799
01:11:25,365 --> 01:11:26,574
VINCENT: You got all the paperwork?

1800
01:11:26,658 --> 01:11:28,660
Wow, that instant stain
remover pen really works.

1801
01:11:28,743 --> 01:11:29,744
-GAIL: Doesn't it?
-Yeah.

1802
01:11:31,829 --> 01:11:34,123
You're back. I like you guys,

1803
01:11:34,207 --> 01:11:35,875
but if you keep coming here
with nothing to offer,

1804
01:11:35,959 --> 01:11:37,835
I'm professionally obligated
to make you sick.

1805
01:11:37,919 --> 01:11:39,295
We have a movie pitch for Jon Hamm.

1806
01:11:39,837 --> 01:11:41,839
What's it about?
Lay it down in two minutes or less.

1807
01:11:41,923 --> 01:11:43,925
Well, Terrence,
I could give you the old verbal pitch.

1808
01:11:44,008 --> 01:11:45,802
That'd be easy.
But I'm gonna do you one better

1809
01:11:45,885 --> 01:11:48,805
because sometimes,
a giant stack of loose paperwork

1810
01:11:48,888 --> 01:11:50,556
is worth a thousand pitches.

1811
01:11:52,475 --> 01:11:54,560
-Is this blood on here?
-Yeah.

1812
01:11:55,395 --> 01:11:56,604
Do you want to explain where it came from?

1813
01:11:56,688 --> 01:11:57,689
No.

1814
01:11:58,314 --> 01:11:59,315
Okay.

1815
01:12:06,614 --> 01:12:07,740
Wow.

1816
01:12:08,491 --> 01:12:11,494
This is the kind of part
Jon Hamm would destroy.

1817
01:12:11,577 --> 01:12:13,830
ALL: (EXCLAIMING) Yes!

1818
01:12:13,913 --> 01:12:16,916
I think it's finally time
for you to meet Mr. Hamm.

1819
01:12:17,000 --> 01:12:18,376
(ALL CHEERING)

1820
01:12:18,459 --> 01:12:20,545
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

1821
01:12:34,517 --> 01:12:36,561
Hey. I'm Jon. What's up?

1822
01:12:36,644 --> 01:12:39,480
Wow. It is such an honor to meet you.

1823
01:12:39,564 --> 01:12:41,649
My name is Gail, and these are my friends.

1824
01:12:42,650 --> 01:12:46,612
-Otto, Caleb, Vincent and...
-Slat-man! I owe you a text.

1825
01:12:46,696 --> 01:12:48,281
Dude, no worries at all.

1826
01:12:48,364 --> 01:12:49,490
It's all good.

1827
01:12:49,574 --> 01:12:52,035
So, my friend Terrence tells me
you guys have a movie to pitch me?

1828
01:12:52,118 --> 01:12:54,287
Yes, we do, and it is a home run.

1829
01:12:54,370 --> 01:12:56,289
Well, it better be, 'cause if it is,

1830
01:12:56,372 --> 01:12:58,374
I will literally do anything for you.

1831
01:12:58,458 --> 01:13:00,335
-I'm gonna hold you to that.
-JON: Okay, and, Slattery,

1832
01:13:00,418 --> 01:13:02,378
-you're gonna be co-starring in this?
-What?

1833
01:13:02,462 --> 01:13:04,630
Don Draper, Roger Sterling,
back together again?

1834
01:13:04,714 --> 01:13:06,132
-Yeah!
-(ALL LAUGHING)

1835
01:13:06,215 --> 01:13:08,009
I'm gonna have to check
my schedule, but yeah.

1836
01:13:08,092 --> 01:13:10,386
Oh, and, Vince here
is an excellent writer.

1837
01:13:10,470 --> 01:13:11,763
He's gonna do the screenplay.

1838
01:13:11,846 --> 01:13:14,974
-Oh, the all-important scribe. Yes, sir.
-(IMITATES TYPEWRITER)

1839
01:13:15,058 --> 01:13:18,186
-(ALL LAUGHING)
-And I assume you are the negotiator?

1840
01:13:18,269 --> 01:13:21,397
Oh, yeah. Well, I worked at CAA
but I'm between agencies at the moment.

1841
01:13:21,481 --> 01:13:24,484
Well, not for long, if this thing does
what I think it's gonna do, am I right?

1842
01:13:24,567 --> 01:13:27,070
Yeah, he's right about that.

1843
01:13:27,570 --> 01:13:28,654
Now, what about my hair?

1844
01:13:28,738 --> 01:13:30,823
Who's gonna take care of that?
Any ideas there?

1845
01:13:30,907 --> 01:13:33,659
Um, you're looking at it.
Three years combined experience.

1846
01:13:34,285 --> 01:13:35,995
Perfect. I am psyched.

1847
01:13:36,579 --> 01:13:38,122
Let's hear this pitch.

1848
01:13:38,206 --> 01:13:40,875
Well, listen, Jonny,
I'd give the old verbal pitch.

1849
01:13:40,958 --> 01:13:42,502
That'd be easy.
But I'm gonna do you one better

1850
01:13:42,585 --> 01:13:45,254
because sometimes,
a binder full of loose paperwork

1851
01:13:45,338 --> 01:13:48,174
-is worth a thousand pitches.
-Okay, but I don't want to read it.

1852
01:13:48,800 --> 01:13:50,885
-You...
-Just tell me the story.

1853
01:13:50,968 --> 01:13:52,387
Tell you... He wants to hear the story.

1854
01:13:52,470 --> 01:13:53,846
-You want me to go?
-CALEB: Oh, yes, yes, yes.

1855
01:13:53,930 --> 01:13:56,474
What do I say? Guys? Guys...
It's a story about espionage.

1856
01:13:57,058 --> 01:13:59,018
Of double identities.

1857
01:13:59,102 --> 01:14:01,646
-A secret global network...
-Okay, let me stop you right there

1858
01:14:01,729 --> 01:14:04,857
'cause I think I get the world of this.
But where's the heart?

1859
01:14:05,358 --> 01:14:07,610
-The heart?
-The heart, the heart.

1860
01:14:07,693 --> 01:14:09,153
That's where your character comes in.

1861
01:14:09,737 --> 01:14:12,198
He's a guy who's been put to the test...

1862
01:14:12,281 --> 01:14:14,784
-Yeah.
-Okay? Until he finally realizes

1863
01:14:14,867 --> 01:14:16,786
what it's all about. The people you love.

1864
01:14:16,869 --> 01:14:19,705
Okay, I like that, but I don't want it
to be too dumbed down.

1865
01:14:19,789 --> 01:14:21,999
Don't you worry about that.
It is the opposite of dumb.

1866
01:14:22,083 --> 01:14:23,626
It blows the lid off the entire genre,

1867
01:14:23,709 --> 01:14:25,628
and it's all centered around
a loose pile of paperwork

1868
01:14:25,711 --> 01:14:27,755
that can't fall into
the wrong hands or else...

1869
01:14:27,839 --> 01:14:28,881
Get this, Jon.

1870
01:14:28,965 --> 01:14:31,217
-Major clusterfuck.
-Clusterfuck. That's smart.

1871
01:14:31,300 --> 01:14:33,469
Okay, so it's smart and it has heart.

1872
01:14:33,553 --> 01:14:35,054
-CALEB: Yes.
-But does it have cojones?

1873
01:14:35,138 --> 01:14:36,931
SLATTERY: Oh, buddy, big ones.

1874
01:14:37,014 --> 01:14:42,395
Try this on for size. One man, two fists,
killing maybe 20, maybe 30 henchmen.

1875
01:14:42,478 --> 01:14:44,272
I don't know,
it felt like the same eight guys

1876
01:14:44,355 --> 01:14:45,523
recycled over and over again.

1877
